+# December 2003 investigative standards and the FAA disposition record
+
+Public derivative of the November 10, 2026 source review UTC · B129 / PD04–PD05, supporting PD01–PD03. The Treasury Inspector General Deskbook reproduces the **December 2003 PCIE/ECIE Quality Standards for Investigations**. The earlier standalone route was unavailable. This government-hosted copy gives contemporaneous wording for investigative file controls, post-investigation records and referral outcomes. The applicable DOT manual, case entries and December 2006 peer-review packet remain open. [December 2003 cover, physical p. 52](https://oig.treasury.gov/system/files/Documents/Inspector%20General%20Deskbook%20Volume%204%20%282%20of%203%29.pdf#page=52)
+
+## What the contemporaneous source adds
+
+| Source locator | Observation and implication for the search |
+| --- | --- |
+| Deskbook part 2, physical **p. 54**, lines **5–30** | The preface includes criminal, administrative and other investigative work within the standards' scope. It describes broad standards and calls for each OIG to issue an investigations manual adapted to its work. Seek the DOT manual, its effective version and case-specific routing or implementation records. [Preface](https://oig.treasury.gov/system/files/Documents/Inspector%20General%20Deskbook%20Volume%204%20%282%20of%203%29.pdf#page=54) |
+| Physical **pp. 64–65**, printed **pp. 10–11** | The interview-note retention sentence at p. 64 lines 29–31 concerns notes prepared in a **criminal investigation**. The separate reporting guideline at p. 65 lines 40–44 addresses exculpatory and relevant mitigating evidence discovered in an **administrative investigation**, with a separate prosecutor provision for criminal and civil matters. The FAA referral's governing case classification and retention authority require their own records. |
+| Physical **pp. 67–68**, printed **pp. 13–14** | The **Case Initiation** subsection covers documenting a decision not to investigate, including referral or no action. The next subsection gives examples of information to track, separating cases closed, referrals to program managers and their outcomes, reports issued, management recommendations and the number of administrative actions. Those fields give independent retrieval targets for **042R0122001 / CC-2006-085**. The separate FAA recommendation to consider action came after the investigation. Whether FAA made or recorded that decision remains unknown. [Case initiation and workload fields](https://oig.treasury.gov/system/files/Documents/Inspector%20General%20Deskbook%20Volume%204%20%282%20of%203%29.pdf#page=67) · [Results fields](https://oig.treasury.gov/system/files/Documents/Inspector%20General%20Deskbook%20Volume%204%20%282%20of%203%29.pdf#page=68) |
+| Physical **pp. 68–69 and 72**, printed **pp. 14–15 and 18** | The case-file section calls for written procedures covering distribution, access records and retention. Appendix A's post-investigative tasks separately include documenting results, dispositions and outcomes, archiving the file and updating the information system with final case information. The standards leave retention periods to applicable requirements. Seek the actual DOT procedure, release or distribution log, file transfer and later case-system updates. [Case-file controls](https://oig.treasury.gov/system/files/Documents/Inspector%20General%20Deskbook%20Volume%204%20%282%20of%203%29.pdf#page=68) · [Post-investigative tasks](https://oig.treasury.gov/system/files/Documents/Inspector%20General%20Deskbook%20Volume%204%20%282%20of%203%29.pdf#page=72) |
+
+The held December 2005 DOT/OST 101 notice independently names referral and action-taken data in TIGR. Together with the 2003 standards, this narrows the search to the case-level export and field history, referral and receipt, and distinct management response. The previously published TIGR record gives **December 12, 2006** as investigation closure. The presence, completeness and contents of further fields remain unverified. [DOT notice, physical p. 2, line 9](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2005-12-21/pdf/E5-7599.pdf#page=2) · [Prior case-status study](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/055ef54a857b46846d0038109bab7e108970f03a/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-postreport-disposition-2026-10-27/README.md)
+
+## Keep the editions and guide records separate
+
+- The December 2003 face names **President's Council on Integrity and Efficiency** and **Executive Council on Integrity and Efficiency**. The November 2011 edition says it supersedes the December 2003 PCIE/ECIE standards. The later Appendix D-1 describes the standards as **“adopted by the CIGIE in December 2003.”** Preserve those statements and the separate **PCIE** and **CIGIE** attributions in the FY 2009 and FY 2010 DOT budget materials. The adoption record and the December 2006 review's actual authority citation would test the relationship. [2003 cover](https://oig.treasury.gov/system/files/Documents/Inspector%20General%20Deskbook%20Volume%204%20%282%20of%203%29.pdf#page=52) · [2011 preface, physical p. 5](https://www.ignet.gov/sites/default/files/files/invprg1211appi.pdf#page=5) · [D-1, physical p. 1, lines 6–7](https://www.ignet.gov/sites/default/files/files/committees/investigation/invprg1211appd1.pdf)
+- The 2003 file provision says **“established immediately upon”** and lists **“File access record.”** The 2011 file provision says **“should be established upon”** and lists **“Access control of the files.”** The later edition also includes electronic file controls and adds calculated savings, if applicable, to the results examples. Both versions contain the same case-initiation sentence about documenting a decision to refer or take no action, verified after joining whitespace. This is a scoped comparison. DOT's operative definitions and application remain open. [2003 physical pp. 67–68](https://oig.treasury.gov/system/files/Documents/Inspector%20General%20Deskbook%20Volume%204%20%282%20of%203%29.pdf#page=67) · [2011 physical pp. 19–21](https://www.ignet.gov/sites/default/files/files/invprg1211appi.pdf#page=19)
+- The Deskbook's **separate** October 2003 general standards cite a **2002 PCIE/ECIE qualitative assessment guide** by title on physical p. 50. The reprinted **GAO-02-437** describes a draft under field testing and gives **April 30, 2002** as the scheduled pilot end. GAO also says the draft recommended sampling closed investigative files. These are a guide citation and a draft/pilot account. The 2002 guide, FY 2006 revision and operative sample criteria remain unacquired. [2002 guide listing](https://oig.treasury.gov/system/files/Documents/Inspector%20General%20Deskbook%20Volume%204%20%282%20of%203%29.pdf#page=50) · [GAO pilot reference, physical p. 8](https://www.gao.gov/assets/gao-02-437.pdf#page=8) · [PCIE revision study](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/80baab1055ee527b4e33a8a3112556f61b49c2e1/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-pcie-peer-review-guide-lineage-2026-11-10/README.md)
+
+## Verification and open records
+
+Two Treasury PDFs were acquired as original hosted responses and three held source PDFs were rehashed. The Deskbook part 2 response is **1,324,114 bytes**, SHA-256 **f22971db1b6b317d53216211bd0689c9d8b5e73002aefd6a98826918a1e8197d**. The check covered **32** PDF text anchors, the scoped shared sentence and the rendered faces of part 2 physical pp. **50, 52, 67, 68 and 72**. The source edition is a reproduction within a compilation. No comparison to a standalone native December 2003 file or full edition-by-edition textual comparison was performed.
+
+- [ ] **PD04–PD05.** Locate the effective DOT OIG investigations manual, TIGR case and post-investigative data dictionary, case distribution and access records, and 2002/FY 2006 guide versions. Obtain the 2006 EPA packet and case worksheets. The records would test how these standards were implemented and whether the case was sampled.
+- [ ] **PD01–PD03.** Obtain the actual correction and delivery evidence, signed consideration/action/no-action decision, and recommendation-specific response, implementation and closeout. A case-initiation decision, investigation closure, report dissemination and management disposition are separately tracked. Keep recommendations **1–2** and **3–4** distinct. [Case-level acquisition queue](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/055ef54a857b46846d0038109bab7e108970f03a/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-postreport-disposition-2026-10-27/OPEN-RECORDS.md)
